course: dictionary
lesson: 6220
title: When words get mixed up
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A misunderstanding happens when you do not understand something correctly, so the message you get is not the message that was meant. «There was a misunderstanding about the time» means two people had different ideas about when to meet.
explain: Sometimes a misunderstanding is small, like a little disagreement. «We had a little misunderstanding» means two friends argued because they did not understand each other. Clearing it up means asking and listening until you both know what was meant.
explain: Look for clues around the word, as you do with any new word. Phrases like «clear up» and «there's been a» tell you that a misunderstanding is a mix-up, not a fight that someone planned.
fact: A misunderstanding is a noun. Its plural is misunderstandings.
fact: «Misunderstanding» comes from the verb «misunderstand», so the -ing form is also «misunderstanding».
fact: «Misunderstanding» means a failure to understand something correctly, or a small argument caused by not understanding each other.
fact: Useful phrases: «clear up a misunderstanding», «there's been a misunderstanding», «a misunderstanding about».
fact: Many arguments start from a misunderstanding, such as a message read in the wrong tone or a mixed-up time or place.
exercise: In «There was a misunderstanding about the time», what is the mix-up about? | *When to meet | Who won the race | The colour of a bike | What to eat for lunch
exercise: What does «We had a little misunderstanding» most likely mean? | A big party with lots of music | A test that everyone passed | *A small argument caused by not understanding each other | A long, quiet walk
exercise: Which phrase means to sort out a mix-up? | *clear up a misunderstanding | lose a game | grow a garden | start a party
test: What does «misunderstanding» mean in «There's been a misunderstanding»? | A big birthday cake | A loud noise in the street | A type of sports game | *A mix-up, where something was not understood correctly
test: How can you clear up a misunderstanding? | Ignore it and hope it goes away | Shout until the other person agrees | *Ask questions and listen carefully | Tell everyone else about it first
exam: Which sentence uses «misunderstanding» correctly? | I misunderstanding the football match in the park. | *We had a misunderstanding about where to meet, so I waited at the wrong gate. | The misunderstanding ate my sandwich on the bus. | Her misunderstanding is a blue bicycle.
